Housing Benefit and Council Tax Benefit performance statistics show that in the first quarter of 2003–4:
96 authorities reported meeting the standard of processing new claims, on average within 36 days;
The average reported number of days to process new claims reduced from 59 in the first quarter of 2002–3 to 53 days in the first quarter of 2003–4;
Authorities in the worst quartile of performance reported processing times between 56 and 153 days;
106 authorities reported meeting the standard of processing changes in circumstances, on average within 9 days;
The average reported number of days to process change of circumstances remains at 18 days when compared to the same quarter in 2002–3.

The FMPR Report is available on the DEFRA website at http://www.defra.gov.uk/wildlife-countryside/issues/common/index.htm, and copies have been placed in the Libraries of both Houses. In summary, the consultant has concluded that:
the functions undertaken by the Commissioners still need to be carried out;
the Commissioners provide a cost effective service;
the functions or the Commissioners should not be transferred to another body at this stage. Once the future role of the Commissioners is clearer, a transfer of responsibilities might be a possibility.

